- runtime/typesol_rt.h, the BigVec section (ts_bigvec_*), and the BigVec<T> layout the compiler gives account data:
  they follow SPL Stake Pool's big_vec.rs (solana-program/stake-pool, program/src/big_vec.rs; earlier in
  solana-labs/solana-program-library), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Changes: rewritten in C and
  TypeScript.

- runtime/typesol_builtins.c, the assembly (__multi3 for SBPF v0; __ashlti3, __lshrti3 and __ashrti3): the
  instructions that the compiler-builtins crate (https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-builtins), as built in
  platform-tools v1.52, has for these functions, written out as assembly so that a program links them from the
  runtime's source. compiler-builtins is licensed "MIT AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND (MIT OR Apache-2.0)"
  (its Cargo.toml); its LICENSE.txt, which says the crate is available under both the MIT licence and the
  Apache-2.0 licence with the LLVM exception and holds both texts, ships verbatim as
  runtime/LICENSE-compiler-builtins.txt (taken from https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-builtins at commit
  8fe310e552c1a24df0bd977e87756168fe396037 of its main branch, on 2026-11-12). Changes: disassembled, labels
  renamed. The division functions in the same
  file are TypeSOL's own C, after the algorithms of Knuth (The Art of Computer Programming, vol. 2, algorithm D) and
  Warren (Hacker's Delight, divlu).

- dist/testing-stake.js (src/testing-stake.ts), stakeActivation: a port of Delegation::stake_activating_and_deactivating_v2
  of solana-stake-interface 4.3.0 (https://github.com/solana-program/stake, interface crate), Copyright Anza
  Maintainers. Licence: Apache-2.0 (the crate's Cargo metadata for 4.3.0; text in test/programs/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt). Changes: rewritten in TypeScript (BigInt arithmetic with the original's u128 saturation).

Third-party material in this repository only (not in the published package)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- test/programs/: program binaries dumped from Solana clusters. The ones kept in the repository are Apache-2.0:
  SPL Account Compression and SPL Noop (solana-labs/solana-program-library), Program Metadata
  (solana-program/program-metadata), coral-xyz/multisig, Raydium CP-Swap, Raydium CLMM and Raydium AMM v4 (raydium-io), Jito's tip
  payment, tip distribution and priority fee distribution programs (jito-foundation/jito-programs), marginfi v2
  (mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2), Solend's token-lending (solendprotocol/solana-program-library) and SPL Stake Pool
  (solana-program/stake-pool); and, under the MIT licence, Phoenix v1 (Ellipsis-Labs/phoenix-v1). The licence texts are test/programs/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt and
  test/programs/LICENSE-MIT-phoenix-v1.txt; each binary's source, program id
  and sha256 are in test/programs/SOURCES.md.
  marginfi v2's Drift v2 test build (drift-labs/protocol-v2) is Apache-2.0 too and kept.
  The Metaplex programs, under the Metaplex(TM) NFT Open Source License 1.0, Kamino's lending and farms programs and
  JupLend's lending, liquidity and rewards programs, under the Business Source License 1.1, and Drift's Merkle
  distributor, under the GNU GPL 3.0, are not kept here: scripts/fetch-programs.sh downloads them.
- showcase/test/fixtures/marginfi/: Marginfi v2's on-chain IDL and three of its mainnet accounts (mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2,
  Apache-2.0), and I80F48 vectors written with the fixed crate (MIT or Apache-2.0).
- showcase/test/fixtures/kamino/: the IDLs of Kamino's lending (1.25.0) and farms programs, the interface descriptions
  as mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2 keeps them in idls-complete/ (Apache-2.0); the programs are not here (see above).
- showcase/test/fixtures/drift/, showcase/test/fixtures/juplend/: the IDLs of Drift v2 and of JupLend's lending,
  liquidity and rewards rate model programs, as mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2 keeps them in idls-complete/ (Apache-2.0).
- showcase/test/fixtures/clmm/: Raydium CLMM's on-chain IDL and the accounts of one mainnet pool (raydium-io/raydium-clmm,
  Apache-2.0).
- showcase/mainnet/: TypeSOL ports of mainnet programs, which follow their originals' source: Raydium CP-Swap, CLMM
  and AMM v4, Jito's MEV programs, marginfi v2, coral-xyz/multisig and SPL Stake Pool (Apache-2.0), and Phoenix v1
  (MIT, Copyright Ellipsis Labs). Every file says which program it ports and under which licence in its first line.
- showcase/mainnet/meteora-dbc/: a TypeSOL port of Meteora's Dynamic Bonding Curve (MeteoraAg/dynamic-bonding-curve,
  release 0.2.2, commit 91e696e), with its tests showcase/test/meteora-dbc*.ts and the mainnet accounts of two of its
  pools and the seven DAMM v2 migration configs those tests read (showcase/test/fixtures/meteora-dbc/; DAMM v2 is under
  the Meteora Noncommercial Licence too). It is not under this repository's MIT
  licence: it is subject to Meteora's Non-commercial Licence, whose text is showcase/mainnet/meteora-dbc/LICENSE.md.
  Required Notice: All underlying software code is subject to the licence set out at https://github.com/MeteoraAg/dynamic-bonding-curve
  The program's mainnet binary is not kept here either, nor are those of DAMM v2 and the locker its migration calls:
  scripts/fetch-programs.sh downloads them (test/programs/SOURCES.md).
- showcase/program-examples/: ports of solana-developers/program-examples (MIT, Copyright Solana Foundation; the
  licence text is in showcase/program-examples/README.md).
